// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-051
=adr: 051
=title: SuperAdmin Module Toggle System
=date: 2026-04-01
=status: accepted

#ctx
ADR-048 gated modules via JWT license keys (HS256/RS256) per subscription.
New model: client (superadmin) controls module access directly via DB toggle.
No per-subscription keys; superadmin is the sole authority across all orgs.
Modules (ADR-049): combustion_dl | asset_life | be_agent
SuperAdmin role: create orgs, create org admins, enable/disable modules. Nothing else.

#opts
opt1: Keep JWT gating — requires key regeneration per change; client cannot self-serve
opt2: DB-backed toggle, SuperAdmin UI — instant enable/disable, no key management

#decision
Singleton ModuleConfig document in MongoDB stores enabled[] array of module identifiers.
SuperAdmin role: PATCH /api/v1/modules → updates enabled[] → persisted to MongoDB.
GET /api/v1/modules (no auth required) → frontend reads current state.
Frontend: useModules() hook replaces useLicense(); reads /api/v1/modules.
KosmosShell, WidgetPalette, NodePalette gate render on module membership in enabled[].
Default on fresh deployment: all modules disabled; superadmin explicitly enables each.
SuperAdmin auth: role='superadmin' on User model; JWT auth middleware enforces PATCH.
One superadmin account seeded at first deployment (credentials set via env or setup wizard).

#consequences
+ Instant enable/disable without image rebuild or key regeneration
+ SuperAdmin self-serves via UI; no CLI, no key files for module control
+ ADR-049 module list and node/widget gating logic unchanged — only the data source changes
- Module state lives in DB; backup/restore must include ModuleConfig document
- If DB wiped, all modules reset to disabled (superadmin re-enables; acceptable)
- ADR-048 JWT license flow deprecated for module gating; ADR-050 RS256 no longer needed

#scope
~supersedes: ADR-048 (module gating), ADR-050 (RS256 for module keys) — both deprecated
~new_backend: ModuleConfig model, ModuleController, module.routes
~new_frontend: useModules hook (replaces useLicense/licenseSlice), SuperAdmin modules page
~affected: KosmosShell, WidgetPalette, NodePalette, licenseSlice → moduleSlice
~user_model: add role field ('superadmin' | 'admin' | 'operator'), seed superadmin on deploy
